  "description": "Filter golden of phase3.2_proc-filter-families (diagnostic): mixed cases on the authored unit cube with edges and corners rounded at radius 0.1 (six UV islands), texture set 1024 px, RGB32F User channels. Every User channel is a fill of the authored content-rgb bitmap (UV projection, tiled 4 x 4, Nearest, so one bitmap texel per texel); User0 is that content alone, and each case adds one content effect on its own channel, the starter-asset filter found by the documented search s:starterassets u:filter n:<name>= with the case's parameters, or the native levels effect: User1 blur-defaults: Blur (defaults); User2 blur-intensity-4: Blur (intensity = 4.0); User3 grayscale-defaults: Grayscale Conversion (defaults); User4 grayscale-bt709: Grayscale Conversion (Red = 0.2126, Green = 0.7152, Blue = 0.0722); User5 grayscale-average: Grayscale Conversion (grayscale_type = 2); User6 sharpen-rgb-defaults: Sharpen (defaults). Painter then bakes World Space Normals low as high (OutputSize 10, LowAsHigh, DilationWidth 0, every other baking parameter at Painter's default) to mark its UV coverage. The User maps and the World Space Normals map are exported as OpenEXR 32f, padding passthrough, no dithering; recorded twice (same session; after save and reopen). Bake backend uncontrolled.",
